diff --git a/docs/MASTER7_FAIL_CLOSED_HARDENING_162.md b/docs/MASTER7_FAIL_CLOSED_HARDENING_162.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4ee7cb6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/MASTER7_FAIL_CLOSED_HARDENING_162.md
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+# MASTER7 v162 fail-closed hardening release
+
+Release: `17.0.0-selfbuilt.162-duitnow-qr-fail-closed`
+
+## Change
+
+- A generic company-bank image no longer counts as DuitNow QR configuration.
+- The DuitNow QR customer entry remains unavailable until the data model and member API expose an explicit, validated QR-specific field.
+- Bank Transfer continues to show every enabled company bank account and its optional bank image.
+- The owner form now identifies the upload as a company-bank image and states that it does not enable DuitNow QR.
+
+## Safety boundary
+
+This release does not create a QR schema, enable manual-bank deposits, approve receipts, credit wallets, call a payment provider, or change any real-money switch. It removes an unsupported readiness inference and keeps the QR path closed.
+
+## Regression
+
+The cashier regression supplies both a generic image and an untrusted client-side `duitnowQrReady` claim. Neither may enable the QR form, while the same accounts remain available through Bank Transfer.
+
+The release also tightens the documentation-only 918KISS MY1 profile diagnostic:
+it requires provider currency `MY1`, settlement currency `MYR`, point units,
+`100:1` provider-to-settlement ratios and the explicit multiply/divide transfer
+direction. USD, USDT, reversed or `1:1` manifests stay incomplete. The adapter,
+wallet and Play capabilities remain disabled regardless of manifest completeness.
+
+The JILI adapter now checks the merchant-contract flag together with each
+independent catalogue, closure and report flag before making a supplier request.
+A lone feature flag cannot reach the transport. Existing runtime evidence still
+has to satisfy the stricter combined gates, and no live supplier call is part of
+this release.
